  "objective": {
    "subject": "feat!: remove thread-pool starvation observation",
    "body": "Delete ParRuntime.openThreadPoolStarvationObservation(Duration),\nThreadPoolStarvationObservationScope, ThreadPoolStarvationReport (with Status\nand Evidence), and ParRuntimeSnapshot.activeObservations(). The runtime no\nlonger creates the ParRuntime-starvation-* sampling scheduler, and the\nshutdown condition, inFlight(), snapshot(), and awaitQuiescence() lose their\nobservation term. The scope only sampled pool-wide ThreadPoolExecutor\ncounters for direct submissions, which executor metrics already export\ncontinuously; the executor wait graph is unchanged. Maintainer decision\nrecorded in design/decision-log.md; migration in the changelog.\n\nContract changes:\n- Removed: design/thread-pool-starvation-observation.md, clauses 1-9 in full\n  (opt-in sampling, interval and evidence rules, status priority, report\n  publication, runtime retention of framework schedulers, Java 8 and\n  interruption rules).\n- Changed: task-group-adopted-futures.md A7 keeps \"adoption MUST NOT wrap,\n  submit, cancel (other than the source), or reorder tasks on the producer\n  pool\" and drops the starvation-sampling complement.\n- Changed: ParRuntime Javadoc for close(), closed(), awaitQuiescence(),\n  inFlight(), and snapshot() no longer name observation scopes; the\n  task-termination-and-scope.md quiescence row follows.\n\nVerification integrity: REVIEWED_EXCEPTIONS records the deleted\nThreadPoolStarvationObservationScopeTest (V1), the two snapshot tests that\nlost their activeObservations assertion (V4), and the renamed adopted-future\ndeadline test (V2), which keeps its deadline and wait-cycle assertions.\n\nassurance: RUN REQUIRED. The diff changes ParRuntime's service-shutdown\ncondition and quiescence accounting, a concurrency-sensitive shared\nmechanism, even though the removed term was always zero for runtimes that\nnever opened an observation."
  },
